<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7173" root="حجر" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحْجِرٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِجْرٌ</span>, in four places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, (S,)
or ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحْجِرٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِحْجَرٌ</span></b> , (K,) The <i>tract surrounding a town</i> or <i>village:</i> (S, K:) [pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحَاجِرُ</span>.]
Hence the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحَاجِر</span> of the kings (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَقْيَال</span>) of ElYemen, which were <i>Places of pasturage,</i> whereof
each of them had one, <i>in which no other person
pastured his beasts:</i> (S, K:) the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">محجر</span> of a
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَيْل</span> of El-Yemen was his <i>tract of land into which
no other person than himself entered.</i> (T.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَجْرَةٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحْجرُ العَيْنِ</span>.

